window.docContents[226].resolve({"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L0-___-The-black-box/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L0-___-The-black-box--Learning-path":{"contents":"* #* Do* Checked by HCP.L0_BlackBox anchor* Concept disclosed\n* 1* In the bare-real oscillator, write the reciprocal quotient under the square root.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#bare_reals* Bare reals do not distinguish the two formulas.\n* 2* Return the tagged potential energy at its declared dimension; inspect both quotient types and try the cross-assignment.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#potential_energy_dimension; HCP.L0_BlackBox#quotient_dimensions* WithDim accepts each quotient at its own dimension and rejects assigning m/k to k/m's type.\n* 3* Pass an angular-frequency value typed as WithDim T𝓭⁻¹ ℝ≥0 to a parameter typed as Frequency.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#frequency_alias* The alias accepts it because the dimensions and carrier types coincide; there is no kind distinction.\n* 4* Decide kind inequality and compare the paired dimensions.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#distinct_kinds_same_dimension* One dimension, two kinds.\n* 5* Try to add kinded angular frequency and frequency.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#refused_kind_addition* The kinded layer refuses cross-kind addition.\n* 6* Put the reciprocal mass/stiffness quotient under a square root in the kinded model.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#refused_reciprocal_radicand* The quotient fails before the square root: no registered edge.\n* 7* Write the L0 system context in prose.* This chapter's System-context card section* State the system boundary and assumptions before adding attributes.\n\nWorksheet: HCP/Worksheets/L0_BlackBox.lean · Solution: HCP/L0_BlackBox.lean\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L0 — The black box","header":"5.1.6. Learning path","id":"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L0-___-The-black-box/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L0-___-The-black-box--Learning-path"},"/The-Proved-Spine/Examination-___-principle___-method___-procedure-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-7___-14_RPAR_/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Examination-___-principle___-method___-procedure-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-7___-14_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\nThe examination chain has three layers — an examination principle (§7.5 / VIM4\n2CD 2.4), a method based on a principle (VIM4 2CD 2.5), and a procedure based\non a method (VIM4 2CD 2.7) — gathered into one carrier ExaminationItem so that refinement\nis a homogeneous relation. The forgetful projection basePrinciple sends any\nitem down to the principle it rests on.\n\nThree small structures with DecidableEq, united by an ExaminationItem\ninductive; basePrinciple is the projection to the principle layer.\n\nAn examination method (Dybkær Ch. 7 / VIM4 2CD 2.5) is a generic description of\nan examination, based on an examination principle.\n\nA structure carrying an identifier and the ExaminationPrinciple it is based on.\n\nAn examination procedure (Dybkær Ch. 7 / VIM4 2CD 2.7) is a detailed description,\nbased on an examination method; its principle is\nthe method's principle.\n\nA structure carrying an identifier and the ExaminationMethod it is based on.\n\nRefinement Refines is the reflexive–transitive closure of the \"based-on\"\nedges (a procedure is based on its method, a method on its principle): procedure\n⊑ method ⊑ principle. It mirrors specialization over\nkinds — the same closure construction, one level down at the defining aspect.\n\nAn inductive with refl and step constructors over a BasedOn edge\nrelation; of_basedOn lifts a single edge.\n\nRefinement is a preorder. It is reflexive (the refl constructor) and\ntransitive (Refines.trans) on the examination chain — the\nsame algebraic law proved for specialization, which an OWL2 reasoner can neither\nstate nor prove.\n\nTransitivity is by induction on the first derivation, exactly as for\nSpecializes: refl returns the second derivation, step re-applies the\nconstructor under the inductive hypothesis.\n\nRefinement preserves the principle. Every examination in one refinement chain\nrests on the same base principle:\n\nThe forgetful projection to the principle layer is invariant along refinement —\nthe examination-layer analogue of  being a homomorphism, and one provable\nhere in the Mathlib-free core without PhysLib. Builds on refinement.\n\nBy induction on the refinement derivation: each BasedOn edge preserves the base\nprinciple (cases … <;> rfl), and the inductive step chains the resulting\nequalities.\n\nThe examination principle is a defining aspect. Two kinds\nexamined by different principles are distinct kinds — independently of scale and\ndimension. This is what keeps width and height distinct while both remain\nrational lengths, mutually comparable under their\nshared super-kind Length.\n\nThe kinds differ in their examPrinciple field, so they are unequal by\ncongruence: substitute the assumed kind-equality and derive a contradiction from\nthe field inequality.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009The Proved Spine","header":"6.4. Examination — principle, method, procedure (Dybkær Ch. 7, 14)","id":"/The-Proved-Spine/Examination-___-principle___-method___-procedure-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-7___-14_RPAR_/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Examination-___-principle___-method___-procedure-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-7___-14_RPAR_"}});